WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.523 --> 00:00:01.624
white house says it believes

00:00:01.757 --> 00:00:03.726
three ufos it shot down this

00:00:03.859 --> 00:00:05.361
weekend were not spying.

00:00:05.494 --> 00:00:07.263
&gt;&gt; Up first for us, though, rage

00:00:07.396 --> 00:00:08.731
and reckoning in Michigan.

00:00:08.864 --> 00:00:12.301
That after a mass shooter leaves

00:00:12.434 --> 00:00:13.802
a killer's imprint on a large

00:00:14.203 --> 00:00:14.270
college campus.

00:00:14.403 --> 00:00:16.205
Three are dead, five more

00:00:16.205 --> 00:00:17.473
wounded critically after a

00:00:17.606 --> 00:00:20.209
gunman hunted students in two

00:00:20.209 --> 00:00:22.344
buildings at Mish misstate.

00:00:22.478 --> 00:00:24.246
The doctors trying to keep them

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:28.684
alive exhausted and emotional.

00:00:28.817 --> 00:00:30.753
&gt;&gt; Can't forget we had general

00:00:30.886 --> 00:00:32.621
surgeons, cardiothoracic

00:00:32.755 --> 00:00:42.231
surgeons, neurosurgeons.

00:00:42.364 --> 00:00:43.866
&gt;&gt; Didn't get a lot of sleep

00:00:44.233 --> 00:00:45.434
last night.

00:00:45.568 --> 00:00:45.734
Sorry.

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:51.574
So many people that just came

00:00:51.707 --> 00:00:51.840
in.

00:00:52.241 --> 00:00:53.108
&gt;&gt; Throughout the morning, some

00:00:53.242 --> 00:00:55.511
new details about the ongoing

00:00:55.644 --> 00:00:56.245
CSI.

00:00:56.245 --> 00:00:59.782
Calls of shots fired came in a

00:00:59.915 --> 00:01:03.219
little before 8:30 last night.

00:01:03.352 --> 00:01:04.587
Police swarmed.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:06.255
Students spent hours locked down

00:01:06.255 --> 00:01:07.189
without knowing whether their

00:01:07.323 --> 00:01:09.191
friends were dead or alive or

00:01:09.325 --> 00:01:10.826
not knowing if the shooter might

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:12.328
walk through their door.

00:01:12.461 --> 00:01:14.263
Today, police putting the name

00:01:14.263 --> 00:01:16.398
to the images of the suspect,

00:01:16.532 --> 00:01:18.267
43-year-old Anthony Mcrae.

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:19.768
The shooter, police say, never

00:01:19.902 --> 00:01:20.636
attended, never taught, and

00:01:20.769 --> 00:01:22.371
never worked at the school.

00:01:22.504 --> 00:01:24.473
Let's get straight to CNN's

00:01:24.607 --> 00:01:26.408
Shimon prokupecz for the latest

00:01:26.542 --> 00:01:26.742
details.

00:01:26.875 --> 00:01:28.410
&gt;&gt; And it appears he is from

00:01:28.544 --> 00:01:29.545
that area, John.

00:01:29.678 --> 00:01:32.281
So that's a significant clue for

00:01:32.381 --> 00:01:33.249
authorities, perhaps he may have

00:01:33.382 --> 00:01:34.617
been to the area before.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.285
Because when you look at the

00:01:36.318 --> 00:01:37.653
surveillance photo that police

00:01:37.786 --> 00:01:38.420
released and some of the

00:01:38.554 --> 00:01:40.289
information that they have been

00:01:40.289 --> 00:01:41.757
releasing, how he went from one

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:42.858
campus, one building to the

00:01:42.992 --> 00:01:44.994
other building, there's some

00:01:45.127 --> 00:01:45.761
indication perhaps that he knew

00:01:45.894 --> 00:01:47.029
where he was going.

00:01:47.162 --> 00:01:47.896
The other significant

00:01:48.297 --> 00:01:49.665
information we're just learning

00:01:49.798 --> 00:01:50.933
from police there in Michigan

00:01:51.066 --> 00:01:52.735
state is that they have

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.970
recovered a note, a note they

00:01:55.104 --> 00:01:57.740
believe that was written by the

00:01:57.873 --> 00:01:59.341
shooter, which will hopefully

00:01:59.475 --> 00:02:00.709
for them shed some light perhaps

00:02:00.843 --> 00:02:03.145
on what happened here, perhaps

00:02:03.279 --> 00:02:04.313
describing some grievances that

00:02:04.413 --> 00:02:05.781
he may have had, some concerns

00:02:05.914 --> 00:02:07.383
that he may have had.

00:02:07.516 --> 00:02:09.752
But again, the motive here

00:02:09.885 --> 00:02:10.786
remains a mystery.

00:02:10.919 --> 00:02:12.321
Police saying this morning

00:02:12.454 --> 00:02:13.589
they're not any closer to

00:02:13.722 --> 00:02:15.291
knowing why he targeted this

00:02:15.424 --> 00:02:15.691
school.

00:02:15.824 --> 00:02:17.660
But this note certainly is going

00:02:17.793 --> 00:02:19.395
to be important for authorities

00:02:19.528 --> 00:02:20.796
as they work through motive and

00:02:20.929 --> 00:02:22.731
try to learn more about this

00:02:22.865 --> 00:02:23.065
gunman.

00:02:23.198 --> 00:02:24.333
What they have been doing, John,

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.001
is they have been talking to

00:02:26.335 --> 00:02:28.337
family members, and others who

00:02:28.337 --> 00:02:30.339
know this gunman, who know the

00:02:30.339 --> 00:02:32.341
shooter, and it sounds like from

00:02:32.341 --> 00:02:33.676
their information, from the

00:02:33.809 --> 00:02:35.878
family, that certain this was a

00:02:36.011 --> 00:02:37.479
troubled individual.

00:02:37.613 --> 00:02:39.281
Family member describing him as

00:02:39.415 --> 00:02:41.550
sort of secluded, kind of to

00:02:41.684 --> 00:02:41.884
himself.

00:02:42.017 --> 00:02:44.353
There was some trouble after his

00:02:44.353 --> 00:02:46.355
mother died, according to his

00:02:46.355 --> 00:02:46.488
father.

00:02:46.622 --> 00:02:48.357
It sounds like for authorities,

00:02:48.357 --> 00:02:50.025
at least, they're learning more

00:02:50.359 --> 00:02:51.660
about the shooter here.

00:02:51.794 --> 00:02:53.729
And at some point, maybe, and we

00:02:53.862 --> 00:02:55.197
may not know ultimately what the

00:02:55.331 --> 00:02:56.799
motive is here, but certainly,

00:02:56.932 --> 00:02:59.134
we hope to hear more from

00:02:59.268 --> 00:02:59.535
authorities.

00:02:59.668 --> 00:03:00.769
Other thing very important here,

00:03:00.903 --> 00:03:02.371
obviously, for the victims, that

00:03:02.504 --> 00:03:03.405
community, and what they're

00:03:03.539 --> 00:03:03.839
going through.

00:03:03.972 --> 00:03:05.407
All of the victims here students

00:03:05.541 --> 00:03:07.376
of the school, the three dead

00:03:07.509 --> 00:03:08.911
and five that remain in the

00:03:09.044 --> 00:03:09.278
hospital.

00:03:09.411 --> 00:03:11.213
You can see the emotion from the

00:03:11.347 --> 00:03:11.547
doctors.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.382
You know, who see all sorts of

00:03:13.515 --> 00:03:16.585
trauma, see all sorts of issues,

00:03:16.719 --> 00:03:18.854
to sort of give that kind of

00:03:18.987 --> 00:03:19.822
emotional statement and to talk

00:03:19.955 --> 00:03:22.391
about it in that way, it tells

00:03:22.391 --> 00:03:24.393
you the effect this is having on

00:03:24.393 --> 00:03:24.827
the community.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.495
&gt;&gt; Without a doubt.

00:03:26.628 --> 00:03:28.030
Shimon prokupecz, appreciate the

00:03:28.397 --> 00:03:28.964
live reporting.

00:03:29.098 --> 00:03:31.800
Let's get expertise from two law

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:32.701
enforcement experts.

00:03:32.835 --> 00:03:34.036
Former deputy director of the

00:03:34.403 --> 00:03:40.409
FBI, Andrew Mccray, and Juliette

00:03:40.409 --> 00:03:41.276
kayyem.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:42.444
There's a lot we don't know, but

00:03:42.578 --> 00:03:45.114
here, Anthony Mcrae, in 2019,

00:03:45.247 --> 00:03:47.216
arrested, charged with a felony

00:03:47.349 --> 00:03:49.451
for carrying a concealed weapon.

00:03:49.585 --> 00:03:50.919
He pleaded to a misdemeanor and

00:03:51.053 --> 00:03:52.621
once his probation was up, his

00:03:52.755 --> 00:03:54.757
probation ended in may 2021.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:57.025
So he had a gun charge on his

00:03:57.159 --> 00:03:57.359
record.

00:03:57.493 --> 00:04:01.764
May 2021, probation ends, then

00:04:01.897 --> 00:04:04.433
you hear his sister calling him

00:04:04.433 --> 00:04:04.500
isolated.

00:04:04.633 --> 00:04:06.435
His father calling him evil

00:04:06.435 --> 00:04:07.536
angry after his mother died.

00:04:07.669 --> 00:04:09.338
Why is the system still unable

00:04:09.471 --> 00:04:10.839
to connect this piece of

00:04:10.973 --> 00:04:12.441
information with this piece of

00:04:12.441 --> 00:04:13.342
information and say this man

00:04:13.475 --> 00:04:14.743
should not have a gun?

00:04:14.877 --> 00:04:16.879
&gt;&gt; Sure, so it comes down to

00:04:17.012 --> 00:04:17.846
those regulations that are

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.782
enshrined in the Brady act of

00:04:19.915 --> 00:04:20.082
1993.

00:04:20.449 --> 00:04:23.285
That sets the parameters for how

00:04:23.419 --> 00:04:24.787
background checks are done for

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.088
gun purposes.

00:04:26.455 --> 00:04:27.756
Michigan is one of most states

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:29.491
that relies on the FBI to

00:04:29.625 --> 00:04:31.293
conduct those background checks.

00:04:31.427 --> 00:04:32.861
In this case, on the facts that

00:04:32.995 --> 00:04:34.897
we know from the reporting about

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:39.134
this man, the arrest for felony

00:04:39.268 --> 00:04:40.769
gun possession had they

00:04:40.903 --> 00:04:42.471
convicted him of felony gun

00:04:42.504 --> 00:04:44.773
possession, might have prevented

00:04:44.907 --> 00:04:47.009
him from ever legally purchasing

00:04:47.142 --> 00:04:48.544
a firearm again.

00:04:48.677 --> 00:04:49.678
Looks like they pled that charge

00:04:49.812 --> 00:04:50.646
to a misdemeanor, and a

00:04:50.779 --> 00:04:51.580
misdemeanor conviction is not

00:04:51.713 --> 00:04:53.048
enough to prohibit you from

00:04:53.182 --> 00:04:54.049
buying a firearm.

00:04:54.483 --> 00:04:56.485
It looks like it was a term in

00:04:56.485 --> 00:04:57.586
his probation he was not allowed

00:04:57.719 --> 00:05:00.022
to have guns while he was on

00:05:00.155 --> 00:05:00.489
probation.

00:05:00.522 --> 00:05:01.890
As you mentioned, he completed

00:05:02.024 --> 00:05:03.225
that probation, so essentially

00:05:03.358 --> 00:05:06.128
after that date, he could, as

00:05:06.495 --> 00:05:07.162
mentally disturbed as he might

00:05:07.296 --> 00:05:09.898
have been, as angry and, you

00:05:10.032 --> 00:05:11.433
know, rage filled as he might

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:13.168
have been, he could walk into

00:05:13.302 --> 00:05:16.138
any federally licensed firearms

00:05:16.505 --> 00:05:17.072
dealer and purchase another gun.

00:05:17.206 --> 00:05:19.475
&gt;&gt; Juliette, you and Andy and I

00:05:19.608 --> 00:05:20.776
have had this conversation far

00:05:20.909 --> 00:05:21.743
too many times.

00:05:21.877 --> 00:05:22.778
Both in your work in government

00:05:22.911 --> 00:05:24.146
and in the private sector, you

00:05:24.513 --> 00:05:25.948
have worked on hardening these

00:05:26.081 --> 00:05:27.916
sites, on improving security on

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:29.284
places that mass shooters

00:05:29.418 --> 00:05:29.618
target.

00:05:29.751 --> 00:05:31.553
Let's listen to one of the many

00:05:31.687 --> 00:05:32.187
survivors here.

00:05:32.521 --> 00:05:34.623
Listen to the fear.

00:05:34.756 --> 00:05:37.993
&gt;&gt; Right when that first gun

00:05:38.126 --> 00:05:39.094
shot went off, I booked to the

00:05:39.228 --> 00:05:40.529
far corner of the class.

00:05:40.529 --> 00:05:42.531
I was sitting right next to the

00:05:42.631 --> 00:05:44.566
door where he came in,

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:46.635
literally, one of the first two

00:05:46.768 --> 00:05:49.571
seats, he came in.

00:05:49.705 --> 00:05:53.041
And I think my fight or flight

00:05:53.175 --> 00:05:54.543
response kicked in because I

00:05:54.543 --> 00:05:55.511
booked to the far side of the

00:05:55.644 --> 00:05:56.545
class and ducked down.

00:05:56.578 --> 00:05:58.547
He aim in and shot three or four

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:00.682
times in our classroom.

00:06:00.816 --> 00:06:02.751
&gt;&gt; Often we're having this

00:06:02.885 --> 00:06:03.519
conversation about elementary

00:06:03.652 --> 00:06:04.553
schools or high schools.

00:06:04.586 --> 00:06:07.256
This is a college campus.

00:06:07.389 --> 00:06:08.557
50,000 students.

00:06:08.557 --> 00:06:10.158
5700 faculty.

00:06:10.559 --> 00:06:11.994
5200 acre campus.

00:06:12.127 --> 00:06:13.862
What can and obviously in this

00:06:13.996 --> 00:06:15.330
case, what can't you do to make

00:06:15.464 --> 00:06:17.065
it safer?

00:06:17.199 --> 00:06:19.468
&gt;&gt; Yeah, I mean, you're

00:06:19.601 --> 00:06:21.737
basically going to have some

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:22.938
level of vulnerability.

00:06:23.071 --> 00:06:25.040
You're not going to be able to

00:06:25.173 --> 00:06:27.943
make these colleges and

00:06:28.076 --> 00:06:29.177
universities safe because

00:06:29.311 --> 00:06:30.212
honestly you don't want them

00:06:30.579 --> 00:06:30.646
safe.

00:06:30.646 --> 00:06:32.748
The kids, they hang out outside.

00:06:32.881 --> 00:06:34.850
They go to concerts, there's

00:06:34.983 --> 00:06:37.419
theaters, sports, classrooms

00:06:37.552 --> 00:06:37.819
themselves.

00:06:37.953 --> 00:06:39.288
What colleges and universities

00:06:39.421 --> 00:06:40.756
are doing are they're trying to

00:06:40.889 --> 00:06:42.858
fortify places where people

00:06:42.991 --> 00:06:44.593
congregate, whether it's a

00:06:44.626 --> 00:06:46.094
classroom or a dorm situation.

00:06:46.228 --> 00:06:48.030
But you're always going to have

00:06:48.163 --> 00:06:49.264
vulnerabilities given the size

00:06:49.398 --> 00:06:49.998
of this.

00:06:50.132 --> 00:06:52.000
And this university, obviously,

00:06:52.134 --> 00:06:53.502
has main streets going through

00:06:53.635 --> 00:06:53.769
it.

00:06:53.902 --> 00:06:55.704
It has bicycles, it's a mini

00:06:55.837 --> 00:06:56.171
city.

00:06:56.605 --> 00:06:57.406
That's a challenge at this

00:06:57.539 --> 00:07:00.676
stage, and we will learn whether

00:07:00.809 --> 00:07:01.677
there were vulnerabilities that

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:03.245
could have been closed by the

00:07:03.378 --> 00:07:05.847
university that may have

00:07:05.981 --> 00:07:06.615
minimized the harm.

00:07:06.615 --> 00:07:07.182
Someone determined to get into

00:07:07.316 --> 00:07:08.884
one of these will likely be able

00:07:09.017 --> 00:07:12.054
to get into one of these

00:07:12.187 --> 00:07:12.621
buildings.

00:07:12.621 --> 00:07:13.355
And that is a challenge.

00:07:13.488 --> 00:07:14.890
I don't mean to be pessimistic

00:07:15.023 --> 00:07:17.125
about it, but what that means is

00:07:17.259 --> 00:07:19.361
then, what we have to do is work

00:07:19.494 --> 00:07:20.963
on what the response capacity

00:07:21.096 --> 00:07:21.596
can be.

00:07:21.997 --> 00:07:23.565
I think you saw a pretty -- sort

00:07:23.699 --> 00:07:25.434
of a near perfect response in

00:07:25.567 --> 00:07:27.636
terms of the surge of resources.

00:07:28.003 --> 00:07:30.872
I did think with kids, this is

00:07:31.006 --> 00:07:32.941
generation lockdown, k-12,

00:07:33.075 --> 00:07:34.643
they're now in college and it's

00:07:34.743 --> 00:07:35.277
following them.

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:36.845
That's what we gave these kids.

00:07:36.979 --> 00:07:38.213
And that's the tragedy of this.

00:07:38.647 --> 00:07:41.249
These are the kids that grew up

00:07:41.383 --> 00:07:42.651
post columbine.

00:07:42.651 --> 00:07:45.253
&gt;&gt; If you go through the

00:07:45.387 --> 00:07:46.989
timeline, first reports shots at

00:07:47.122 --> 00:07:47.422
8:30.

00:07:47.756 --> 00:07:50.659
A suspect description tweeted at

00:07:50.692 --> 00:07:51.026
9:39.

00:07:51.159 --> 00:07:53.028
Suspect located and died of a

00:07:53.161 --> 00:07:55.897
self-inflicted gunshot wound at

00:07:56.031 --> 00:07:56.198
11:35.

00:07:56.331 --> 00:07:57.632
To your point, generation

00:07:57.766 --> 00:07:58.867
lockdown, they put out a

00:07:59.001 --> 00:08:01.069
photograph, and they get a tip

00:08:01.203 --> 00:08:02.671
pretty quick.

00:08:02.671 --> 00:08:04.806
So it sounds demented to say

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:06.675
this, they did the best they

00:08:06.675 --> 00:08:07.743
could under horrific

00:08:07.876 --> 00:08:08.677
circumstances.

00:08:08.677 --> 00:08:10.012
&gt;&gt; They did the best, that's

00:08:10.145 --> 00:08:10.312
right.

00:08:10.679 --> 00:08:11.380
Your standards in my world are

00:08:11.513 --> 00:08:12.814
can we make it less bad?

00:08:12.948 --> 00:08:14.950
I think the university really

00:08:15.083 --> 00:08:15.217
did.

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:18.687
Their preplanning with the

00:08:18.687 --> 00:08:19.955
locals and then the state and

00:08:20.088 --> 00:08:23.291
then we saw federal assets come

00:08:23.425 --> 00:08:24.092
in seemed perfect.

00:08:24.292 --> 00:08:26.695
I wanted to pick up on one point

00:08:26.695 --> 00:08:28.697
we often don't talk about,

00:08:28.797 --> 00:08:29.097
communication.

00:08:29.231 --> 00:08:30.332
I was monitoring in real time.

00:08:30.699 --> 00:08:31.600
They're doing everything you

00:08:31.733 --> 00:08:32.968
would want to do, which is get

00:08:33.101 --> 00:08:34.703
to the students, tell them what

00:08:34.703 --> 00:08:36.705
to do, get to the faculty and

00:08:36.705 --> 00:08:37.906
then colleges and universities,

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.508
these are kids still.

00:08:39.641 --> 00:08:41.143
And get to the parents, and

00:08:41.276 --> 00:08:42.978
telling the parents, do not come

00:08:43.111 --> 00:08:46.715
to campus because it's a danger

00:08:46.848 --> 00:08:47.649
zone, so to speak.

00:08:47.783 --> 00:08:50.919
All of that is so important in

00:08:51.053 --> 00:08:52.721
that timeline that we saw.

00:08:52.721 --> 00:08:54.990
How short it was, was because

00:08:55.123 --> 00:08:56.124
everyone knew what to do.

00:08:56.258 --> 00:08:57.993
&gt;&gt; Andy Mccabe, as you're trying

00:08:58.126 --> 00:08:59.261
to answer the question why, to

00:08:59.394 --> 00:09:01.430
get to a motive, the police on

00:09:01.563 --> 00:09:02.731
campus say no connection.

00:09:02.731 --> 00:09:03.799
Didn't go to school there,

00:09:03.932 --> 00:09:05.500
didn't teach there, didn't work

00:09:05.634 --> 00:09:05.801
there.

00:09:05.934 --> 00:09:07.836
But did, as Shimon noted, have a

00:09:07.969 --> 00:09:09.771
note in his pocket, apparently,

00:09:09.905 --> 00:09:11.173
threatening some schools in new

00:09:11.306 --> 00:09:11.506
Jersey.

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:13.809
How do you try to piece together

00:09:13.942 --> 00:09:14.076
why?

00:09:14.209 --> 00:09:17.379
Why this gunman decided to go to

00:09:17.512 --> 00:09:18.747
this campus late in the evening

00:09:18.747 --> 00:09:21.416
and open fire.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:21.950
&gt;&gt; John, we do this

00:09:22.084 --> 00:09:23.218
investigation only for that

00:09:23.351 --> 00:09:23.552
reason.

00:09:23.685 --> 00:09:25.220
There's no one to charge here.

00:09:25.353 --> 00:09:25.887
He's dead.

00:09:26.021 --> 00:09:27.823
He's not going to jail.

00:09:27.956 --> 00:09:29.357
But people have a desperate need

00:09:29.491 --> 00:09:30.225
to know why.

00:09:30.358 --> 00:09:32.194
Why this place, why these

00:09:32.327 --> 00:09:33.361
victims, why this night.

00:09:33.495 --> 00:09:34.796
And so what the investigators

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:36.798
will do is they'll go back and

00:09:36.932 --> 00:09:38.366
execute search warrants at his

00:09:38.767 --> 00:09:39.868
residence, maybe on his

00:09:40.001 --> 00:09:42.003
vehicles, they'll look in all

00:09:42.137 --> 00:09:44.039
his electronic devices, they're

00:09:44.172 --> 00:09:46.041
course through if he has ever

00:09:46.174 --> 00:09:47.275
used social media, what sort of

00:09:47.409 --> 00:09:48.977
things he's powed or said or

00:09:49.111 --> 00:09:49.344
liked.

00:09:49.478 --> 00:09:51.012
They'll look at all his

00:09:51.146 --> 00:09:51.980
writings, try to interview

00:09:52.114 --> 00:09:53.381
family members and friends and

00:09:53.515 --> 00:09:54.916
work associated all to answer

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:56.785
that question of why.

00:09:56.785 --> 00:09:58.787
Maybe we'll get an answer, maybe

00:09:58.854 --> 00:09:59.454
we won't.

00:09:59.588 --> 00:10:01.756
The other question we should be

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:02.791
asking is how.

00:10:02.791 --> 00:10:03.492
How does this happen?

00:10:03.625 --> 00:10:07.462
How does it happen 60 or so

00:10:07.596 --> 00:10:08.797
times this year alone?

00:10:08.797 --> 00:10:10.799
And the answer is because we

00:10:10.799 --> 00:10:12.200
have 120 guns in this country

00:10:12.334 --> 00:10:13.635
for every 100 people.

00:10:13.768 --> 00:10:17.239
We have more than double the

00:10:17.372 --> 00:10:17.939
number of the second most gun

00:10:18.073 --> 00:10:19.174
soaked country on Earth, which

00:10:19.307 --> 00:10:20.976
is Yemen, not some place I think

00:10:21.109 --> 00:10:23.278
we should be comparing ourselves

00:10:23.411 --> 00:10:23.545
to.

00:10:23.678 --> 00:10:25.213
Every lawful gun owner in this

00:10:25.347 --> 00:10:27.182
country of which I am one, I

00:10:27.315 --> 00:10:28.817
carried a gun every day for 21

00:10:28.817 --> 00:10:30.452
years on the job, I own a

00:10:30.819 --> 00:10:32.020
firearm, every lawful gun owner

00:10:32.154 --> 00:10:33.054
should stand up and say enough

00:10:33.188 --> 00:10:33.788
is enough.

00:10:33.922 --> 00:10:35.891
We need actually effective laws,

00:10:36.024 --> 00:10:37.292
actually effective background

